     "result_text_tail": "yout checks reported no problems, but I couldn't preview the slides visually (no PowerPoint converter here), so give them a look in PowerPoint.\n- An independent reviewer recomputed 32 numbers and found no arithmetic errors. I applied its other points:\n  - wording fixes on several titles;\n  - a test of what happens if only half the 2027 volume arrives (the base case ends slightly negative);\n  - the Japan-first-then-US option, now sized in numbers;\n  - an ad-cost assumption in the retail evidence case that matches the base case.\n- Of the 12 hypotheses tested, 2 were confirmed, 6 revised and 4 refuted.\n- Model results such as cash flows and margins are calculations from the planning team's inputs. Only four numbers are marked as my own estimates.\n\n**Choices I made on your behalf**\n- A deep deck (about 40 slides) for the CEO and board, who approve or reject entry and choose the route.\n- The navy theme.\n- The pilot's 28% as the base-case ad cost, because the plan's 25% is below the benchmark range; the 32% benchmark plus a 25% duty is the stress case.\n- One-time costs expensed in the year they're spent.\n- Mass retail, brand websites and currency effects left out because the pack has no inputs for them; they're listed on the appendix's \"what we did not pursue\" page.\n\nPossible next steps: turn the half-2027-volume test into a full scenario, try another theme, or add speaker notes.\n\nFiles are in `deliverable/`:\n- onsoo-us-entry.pptx\n- onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx\n- onsoo-us-entry.json"
    }
